### 3.4 Design Constraints
Document standards compliance, technology decisions, and architectural constraints.

### 3.5 Software System Attributes
#### 3.5.1 Reliability
Define reliability targets (e.g., uptime, MTBF, error handling expectations).

#### 3.5.2 Availability
Describe availability objectives and failover expectations.

#### 3.5.3 Security
Outline authentication, authorization, data protection, and audit requirements.

#### 3.5.4 Maintainability
Describe maintainability goals (e.g., modularity, documentation, logging).

#### 3.5.5 Portability
Specify portability or deployment requirements.

### 3.6 Logical Database Requirements
Document data entities, schemas, and persistence expectations.

### 3.7 Design and Implementation Constraints
Capture programming languages, tools, and design patterns that must be used or avoided.

### 3.8 Software Quality Attributes
Summarize non-functional attributes and quality goals.

## 4. Verification
